#
# Site notes: context the code doesn't show (findings, decisions), as of 15 Nov 2026.
#
# Why start.gg:
# - supermajor.gg player pages turn automated clients away since Nov 2026 (see the Site notes
#   in ds/data/raw/supermajor.py). start.gg is where that data comes from, and it has an
#   official API, so we rebuild the stats from sets ourselves.
# - Own client, no SDK: the Python wrappers on PyPI are stale (`startgg` pins pydantic<2,
#   `startggapi` 2023, `pysmashgg` 2022) or sync with fixed queries (`pystartgg`), and the API
#   is one endpoint. Third-party MCP servers exist too; not used, because they would hand the
#   agent results (see "Results" below) and skip our char ids.
#
# How the API behaves (limits from the docs; the rest measured with scripts/startgg_probe.py
# on 15 Nov 2026 for Sparg0 and rm8, 150 newest sets each):
# - Tokens expire a year after they are created: a token that worked and now gets "rejected
#   the API token" most likely just needs replacing (`ds settings sync`).
# - Limits: 80 requests per 60 s on average, and 1000 objects per request, nested objects
#   included. Over the first: `{"success": false, "message": "Rate limit exceeded ..."}`.
#   Over the second: `"Query complexity too high. ... (actual: 1235)"`. The count is of the
#   real response, not an estimate: 60 sets came to 2000 objects for Sparg0 and 1913 for rm8,
#   about 33 per set with the PLAYER_SETS selection, so 29-31 average sets fit. Pages vary
#   a lot (best-of-5 sets): 25 and 20 per page both went over for Sparg0, so api.PER_PAGE
#   is 15, which never did.
# - `Player.sets` has no videogame filter and no date filter, so api.player_sets pages newest
#   first and stops at the cutoff, dropping other games' sets by `event.videogame.id`.
# - Player ids: supermajor's `S<digits>` id is the start.gg player id with an `S` in front
#   (S158026 -> 158026 Sparg0, S1006473 -> 1006473 rm8; both returned the same tag).
# - Coverage, which varies by who reports the bracket:
#   - Games reported at all: 82-86% of sets. The rest have only a set score.
#   - Characters: 99-100% of reported games have both players' characters.
#   - Winner per game: 100% of reported games.
#   - Stage: 34% of games for Sparg0, 0% for rm8. Stage stats will often be thin or empty.
#   - VOD link: about 1% of sets (1 of 150, and 0 of 150). VOD search will rarely find much.
# - The cap decides the window for busy players: rm8's 150 newest sets cover 6 weeks, Sparg0's
#   cover 4 months. Say the real span, not "last 6 months".
# - Speed: 150 sets took 3-4 s at 15 per page (13-17 requests, 4 in parallel).
# - Cost per lookup (15 Nov 2026, from the call log): a usage lookup is ONE start.gg request
#   (queries.USAGE_SETS, 30 sets, singles only; the character list is stored in code, see
#   ds.data.raw.startgg.characters), plus supermajor's tag search for a tag. It used to be the
#   newest 150 sets: 14 requests for Sparg0, 18 for rm8. player_sets fetches the character
#   list once per call when not given it; it used to fetch it per page, which the old disk
#   cache hid.
# - `entrantSize: [1]` in SetFilters (not in the docs' examples, works) returns 1v1 sets only:
#   doubles were 13-15% of a player's sets. There is no videogame filter (`videogameIds` is
#   rejected), so other games still come back: 7 of 30 for Sparg0, 1 of 30 for rm8.
# - One request of 30 sets is 23-29 Ultimate sets, 3-4 events (Sparg0 Oct 24 to Nov 13, rm8
#   Nov 3 to 11); two are about 48 sets, 6-7 events. Each event is 4-10 sets.
# - Character names that are not one char.parquet id: 'Pokemon Trainer' and 'Pyra & Mythra'
#   (group ids 'pokemon_trainer' / 'pyra_mythra', see spec/pkgs/ds/data/external_sources.md)
#   and 'Random Character' (no char_group). 'Rosalina' and 'Simon Belmont' don't match ours
#   by name (api.SITE_CHARACTER maps them; found by `ds data startgg-char`).
# - All eight queries in queries.py ran without a schema error.
#
# Decisions:
# - Results (who won, scores, placements, seeds) ARE returned by this package: the user wants
#   the data layer complete. The limit is on the agent only: ds.ai.startgg exposes no result
#   field, function or parameter. Don't strip results here, and don't add them there.
# - Snappy over complete: callers ask for a capped recent window, never all-time.
# - No caching, by the user's decision (15 Nov 2026; the disk cache was removed): every call
#   asks start.gg. See "Caching Policy" in .agents/agents.md before adding any.
# - Standing live test players: Sparg0 (normally active) and rm8 (very many sets a year, the
#   cap test). Test prompt for the agent: "get stats for Sparg0".
